## <a id="english">English</a>

### 1. Purpose

Orbis Agent prioritizes local storage of data on the user's device to reduce leakage risk and improve user control.

### 2. Retention Period

- Configuration data is typically retained when the user makes changes
- Application state data is retained as needed for user workflows or personalization
- Unnecessary data is removed when a feature is disabled or cleanup is performed

### 3. No Unwanted External Storage

We do not retain user data on external servers unless:

- The user explicitly agrees
- A feature requires integration with an external service
- There is a legal or security necessity requiring retention

### 4. Deletion of Data

Users may delete saved data to clean up or disconnect from related services. In cases involving external services, data handling follows that service's terms.

### 5. Updates

We may update this data retention policy as new features are introduced or security processes change.
